<title> Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item> 5.8.1: Meaning of a Function Presented Graphically </item>
  <item> 5.8.2: Represent a Function as a Table of Values, Graph, and Equation <list>
      <item> 5.8.2: Self Check </item>
      <item>Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item> 5.8.3: Using Function Language and Notation <list>
      <item> 5.8.3: Self Check </item>
      <item>Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item> 5.8.4: Function Notation </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 5.8.5: Practice.</para>
<title> Required Materials</title>
<para>Graphing technology</para>
<title> Required Preparation</title>
<para>Devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology should be available as an option for students to select during the lesson. It is ideal if each student has their own device.</para>
<title> Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. <span>Encourage students to look for these words and notice their use and meanings.</span></item>
  <item> Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations. </item>
  <item> Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link> </item>
</list>
